From: matanco64 <38103422+matanco64@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Don't call OnMainThread() from the main thread in macdrv_update_opengl_context().

macdrv_update_opengl_context() is reached from -[WineContentView viewWillDraw] on the
main thread when a context was still pending at the time the view became visible. The
"update" branch then calls OnMainThread(), which queues the block for the main run loop
and waits on a semaphore forever -- behind its own wait, since the main thread is the one
waiting. The window stops being serviced (spinning cursor) and every Wine thread that
needs the main thread hangs with it.

Observed with an application that attaches an OpenGL context to a window already hosting
a Metal-backed (D3DMetal) swap chain. The two other OnMainThread() call sites in this
file already guard with -[NSThread isMainThread]; do the same here.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
index 2801834..b6ee50c 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
@@ -319,6 +319,8 @@ void macdrv_update_opengl_context(macdrv_opengl_context c)
                 [context clearDrawableLeavingSurfaceOnScreen];
                 context.view = view;
             }
+            else if ([NSThread isMainThread])
+                [context update];
             else OnMainThread(^{
                 [context update];
             });
